    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE — `@m0saic/charts/stat-card/v1`** (gate 17 — CLOSES THE CHARTS PACK 4/4; chart: `.ai/LAUNCH/v1-template-cut.md`). Props = showcase defaults. Alpine/stat-card/v1 already shipped base (gate 10) — this is the original it forked from.\n\n| Stage | Current | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Flags | not internal, not deprecated, primitive:true | confirm |\n| Gate | — | **base** |\n| Preview assets | see history note | review |\n| Cover / Tutorial | cover BUILT this gate (count-up + cascade starts near-blank) | eyeball cover; tutorial needed? |\n\n**Pre-audit found + fixed 3:**\n1. **The CARD RENDERED BLACK through the .mosaicx path** — the design deliberately made the surface doc.backgroundColor-only (\"single flat layer\"), which the known bg-drop candidate (2026-08-06) strips at template_invocation flattening. Verified by pixel: the whole battery's cards were (0,0,0). Surface now ALSO paints as a real base tile (\"none\" keeps the flat transparent doc).\n2. **No text caps anywhere** — the VALUE is a FIXED-fontSize expr layer (no fit): a 13-char value at H·0.46 clipped to \"1,248,9\" at 640×360; label/delta/sublabel (fit:contain) clipped in the CLI too. Ported the alpine stat-card capFont + fitTo idiom, script-aware, all four groups.\n3. **Band-height arrow dwarfed the text at portrait aspects** (122px triangle vs 10px text at 360×640) — ported alpine's two-pass arrow cap (arrow ≤ 1.5× delta font, re-derive cells; byte-identical at the ideal ~2.6:1).\n\nAlso: debugLayout contract (4 textFits groups; debug forces the literal value/flare so coverage is unconditional — the donut pattern), tagged sources, cover (inline-flat, probed cell).\n\n**Primitive-sense: KEEP primitive:true** — the KPI building block the repo-tracker hero composes 4×.\n\nBattery 84/84 baseline (feasibility-green, VISUALLY broken: black cards + clipped text) + 84/84 final build ×2, probe 14/14 defaults + 70/70 binding configs (13-char value, Cyrillic, no-delta, custom bg, none+noslide), jest 10/10 (indices shifted for the base tile).",
